		"The 50 regular cards were transcribed from their official Japanese Pokémon Card Game detail pages; each page URL and SHA-256 digest is listed below.",
		"The five secret-numbered cards were checked against card scans in the cited independent checklist. Cards 051–053 match the gameplay text and stats of the cited regular BW5a cards; cards 054 and 055 use the matching official Reuniclus and Rayquaza gameplay records, with scan-verified card identity, illustrator and rarity.",
		"The independent checklist header reports 54 cards (50 regular and 4 secret), but its numbered entries continue through 055/050. The cited Japanese BW checklist independently totals 55 (24 Common, 16 Uncommon, 10 Rare, 3 SR, 2 UR), so the data contains all 55 printed-number identities while the official set denominator remains 50.",
		"Each card has first-edition and unlimited variants. Official per-card rarity and the independent edition checklist distinguish 40 normal cards (Common/Uncommon) from 15 holo cards (Rare/SR/UR). No reverse-holo variants are included.",
		"SR is mapped to Ultra Rare and UR to Secret Rare following the neighboring Japanese BW set data. No marketplace IDs or unverified artwork URLs are included; secret scan URLs are provenance only."
	],
